## Assessment — 20260905-strategic-outcomes-verify

### What this cycle actually did (verified, not claimed)

The executor cycle under assessment produced **zero work**. `coo/tmp/20260905-strategic-outcomes-verify.exec.log` shows a harness-level failure: `num_turns: 0`, session `ff46aaab…`, "Exec ended early: insufficient permission to proceed. Re-run with --auto medium or --auto high." No outcome block was appended to the tangent file, no LLM spend occurred, and no file anywhere was modified (strategic_review.py mtime 2026-08-24 17:11:47; proposals mtime 2026-08-09; both artifacts it should have produced — `.run.log`, `.guard-check.out` — do not exist). The outcome note at `coo/outcomes/…verify.md` predates this cycle (21:33 vs exec claim 21:39) and belongs to the prior partial cycle.

### Root cause — runner misconfiguration, not executor error

- `coo-loop-v4.sh` `do_execute` launches `droid execute exec -o json -f "$f"` with **no `--auto` flag**, while scope runs `--auto high` and assess/validate run `--auto medium` (both of which demonstrably execute commands fine). The executor's required actions (run the python proof, write logs) need at least medium approval. The failure is deterministic.
- Corroboration: `20260905-ntreis-fm23`'s executor died identically twice tonight (`num_turns: 0`, same gate) under the same invocation class.
- Continuity machinery is also broken: the loop greps exec.log for `"sessionId"` but the JSON emits `"session_id"`, so `executor_session:` was never persisted into the tangent file. A RELOOP would therefore silently start a **fresh** session through the identical broken invocation — the defining property of reloop (same-session continuation) cannot be realized.

