The failure is environmental in origin, but the RELOOP mechanism cannot deliver its semantics here: session continuity was never persisted (grep bug), and a fresh or resumed executor invocation deterministically re-hits the same permission gate before any turn. "Plausibly achievable within remaining budget_cycles" therefore fails for the only path available — a second run would be a known-deterministic failure (the exact pattern the rules route to RESCOPE after the fact). The contract's execution mechanism, not its goal, is what's broken; reissue with evidence is the honest disposition.

